# Thin per-repo CI Dockerfile, derived from the canonical
# .codespace/docker/node-ci/Dockerfile.ci.template. FROM the digest-pinned
# shared node-ci base (the single source of the validation toolchain and of the
# entrypoint that executes .local-ci.yml), then copy the repo.
#
# The base is DIGEST-PINNED (@sha256:...) — never a floating tag — so the build
# is reproducible and local==CI image identity holds. The pin below is the same
# node-ci version every other managed repo in this estate is on.
#
# DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE FROM THE TEMPLATE — do not "restore" the template here.
# The template's `COPY package.json package-lock.json .npmrc ./`, its `npm ci`
# layer, and its `--mount=type=secret,id=NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` branch all exist to
# install Node dependencies, routing private `@richardwilliams/*` packages to
# GitHub Packages. This repo has NO package.json, NO lockfile, NO .npmrc and no
# dependencies of any kind — it ships YAML manifests, two shell scripts and
# documentation. COPYing nonexistent files is a hard build failure, and an npm
# install layer for a repo with nothing to install is pure machinery. Hence the
# single COPY below and no install step.
#
# What this image IS used for: the base provides bash and the runner that reads
# .local-ci.yml, which is what the validation steps need. Restore the template's
# npm shape only if this repo ever gains real Node dependencies.
#
# THE ONE ADDED LAYER — python3-yaml. The gates read the app manifest, the
# compose file and the vendored deployment contract with a real parser rather
# than by grepping structured documents. The base image carries python3 but no
# YAML parser at all, and carries neither `jq` nor `yq`, so python3 plus PyYAML
# is the only parser both this image and the operator's machine are guaranteed
# to have. Installed from apt rather than pip because the base ships a
# distribution python3, and the lists are cleaned in the same layer so the image
# does not carry an apt cache.
#
# THE VERSION IS PINNED, and the pin is load-bearing rather than tidiness. The
# base above is digest-pinned so that local and CI are identical BY
# CONSTRUCTION, which is the whole of INVARIANTS.md § Local CI Equivalence; an
# unpinned `apt-get install` on top of it resolves against Ubuntu's live archive
# at build time, so two builds of this same file can land different PyYAML
# versions. PyYAML is what `scripts/lib/manifest_data.py`'s folded-scalar
# emitter runs on, and `scripts/release.sh` and
# `scripts/check-release-notes-drift.sh` share that emitter — so a folding
# change between versions gives the drift gate the same wrong-against-wrong
# blindness it exists to prevent, except split across two machines: the gate
# passes on each while they write different bytes into the manifest.
#
# 6.0.1-2build2 is what the pinned base's noble/main resolves to, verified
# identical on arm64 and amd64 so the pin holds for both the operator's machine
# and the amd64 CI runner.
#
# WHEN UBUNTU DROPS THIS VERSION THE BUILD WILL FAIL, LOUDLY. That is the
# correct behaviour and it is not a defect to route around: do NOT unpin, and
# do NOT float the version to make the red go away. Either resolve the new
# version the pinned base offers and update the pin here, or move PyYAML into
# the shared node-ci base image, where its own digest pin guarantees the version
# for every repo at once. Both keep the by-construction identity; unpinning
# trades it for a green build.
FROM ghcr.io/richardwilliams/node-ci:v0.1.3@sha256:5409e3507f25fa391f9b19cb827ffb818808931b166802881f8dc7ee7a22fc92
RUN apt-get update \
 && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends python3-yaml=6.0.1-2build2 \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
